  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fifth prerelease; the public API is 0.4.0-alpha's. New: the keys the original interpreters kept for themselves, as ScummVM has them (but on the NES): Space pauses, the game, its clock and sound standing still until a key or a click; F8 asks before restarting; F6 turns the sound off and on; Ctrl+C and Alt+X quit. Fixed: in the C64 demo, the inspector lists only its rooms (not those on the disk it lacks, nor costume-only rooms), and F5 does nothing instead of throwing. The maniacal tool has the mansion for its icon, opens its window as large as fits the display, names the release in its title bar, and steers the cursor from the arrow keys and the numpad (5 clicks; 1, 3, 7 and 9 jump to the corners).",
